DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
6493::$$$message_0048_0000_0000$$$::Caster's here.[lr]::
6494::$$$message_0048_0000_0001$$$::...She stands around thinking an awful lot. I wonder if something's been bothering her lately.::
6495::$$$message_0048_0001_0000$$$::"She turned me down the last time I came to ask about the Holy Grail War..."[lr]::
6496::$$$message_0048_0001_0001$$$::But maybe, just maybe...[lr]::
6497::$$$message_0048_0001_0002$$$::she might finally reveal a bit of the truth to me.::
6498::$$$message_0048_0002_0000$$$::Ha. Ask Caster to tell me the whole truth?[lr]::
6499::$$$message_0048_0002_0001$$$::Fat chance.[lr]::
6500::$$$message_0048_0002_0002$$$::I already asked Caster everything I could.[lr]::
6501::$$$message_0048_0002_0003$$$::If I try to pry any more answers out of that witch, it would be asking her to tell me the actual truth behind this whole situation.[lr]::
6502::$$$message_0048_0002_0004$$$::That's too reckless. She might be enjoying domestic life now, but she's a genuine witch.[lr]::
6503::$$$message_0048_0002_0005$$$::She won't hesitate to eliminate anyone who doesn't benefit her.[lr]::
6504::$$$message_0048_0002_0006$$$::Like swatting a housefly.::
6505::$$$message_0048_0003_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
6506::$$$message_0048_0003_0001$$$::I can't let my guard down.[lr]::
6507::$$$message_0048_0003_0002$$$::If I'm to survive around someone who lived her life hurting others, the worst mistake I could make is to let her think I'm someone she can take advantage of.::
6508::$$$message_0048_0004_0000$$$::"...Yeah. This is the traitorous witch Medea we're talking about.[lr]::
6509::$$$message_0048_0004_0001$$$::An Anti-Hero who's been enshrined as an enemy of humans..."[lr]::
6510::$$$message_0048_0004_0002$$$::I recall her story from Greek mythology: [lr]::
6511::$$$message_0048_0004_0003$$$::A princess who studied under a powerful witch.[lr]::
6512::$$$message_0048_0004_0004$$$::She gained infamy for plotting the downfall of many ancient nations during the Age of Gods.::
6513::$$$message_0048_0005_0000$$$::Princess Medea.[lr]::
6514::$$$message_0048_0005_0001$$$::Daughter of King Aeetes of Colchis, an ancient Greek kingdom said to have been located on the eastern shore of the Black Sea.[lr]::
6515::$$$message_0048_0005_0002$$$::She was a priestess of Hecate, the goddess of magecraft, and a pampered princess who was adored by the king.[lr]::
6516::$$$message_0048_0005_0003$$$::She was born into a blessed environment and lived a happy life, ignorant of the outside world.[lr]::
6517::$$$message_0048_0005_0004$$$::Yearning for neither freedom nor adventure,[lr]::
6518::$$$message_0048_0005_0005$$$::she loved her homeland and was content to live and die in its hills.::
6519::$$$message_0048_0006_0000$$$::   Unfortunately...[lr]::
6520::$$$message_0048_0006_0001$$$::Young Medea's dream would be dashed when heroes arrived on the shores of Colchis seeking fortune and glory.[lr]::
6521::$$$message_0048_0006_0002$$$::Jason, captain of the ship Argo.[lr]::
6522::$$$message_0048_0006_0003$$$::Seeker of the Golden Fleece, a national treasure of Colchis, and the one to influence Medea to betray her country.[lr]::
6523::$$$message_0048_0006_0004$$$::The goddess Aphrodite, who favored Jason, cursed Medea to fall madly in love with him.::
6524::$$$message_0048_0007_0000$$$::Medea betrayed her father the king, gave the Golden Fleece to Jason, married him, and fled Colchis.[lr]::
6525::$$$message_0048_0007_0001$$$::The king pursued the Argo in search of his daughter, but the cursed Medea murdered her younger brother with magecraft and scattered his remains in the sea.[lr]::
6526::$$$message_0048_0007_0002$$$::While the king mournfully gathered his son's remains, Jason and his band took the time to escape.::
6527::$$$message_0048_0008_0000$$$::The threat left the eastern Black Sea...[lr]::
6528::$$$message_0048_0008_0001$$$::...but disquiet would haunt the Argo for the rest of its days.[lr]::
6529::$$$message_0048_0008_0002$$$::She was the princess who handed over her nation's treasure to a man.[lr]::
6530::$$$message_0048_0008_0003$$$::The woman who killed her own brother for the man she loved.[lr]::
6531::$$$message_0048_0008_0004$$$::The heroes aboard the Argo reviled the princess of Colchis and spread her infamy.::
6532::$$$message_0048_0009_0000$$$::Seeing her as repulsive and filthy, they shunned her.[lr]::
6533::$$$message_0048_0009_0001$$$::Fortunately, perhaps, Medea's heart was too enraptured by the goddess's curse for the men's critical gazes to be more than a passing sea breeze to her.[lr]::
6534::$$$message_0048_0009_0002$$$::She was happy as long as she had Jason's words.::
6535::$$$message_0048_0010_0000$$$::"Sorry about that. But you did well, Medea."[lr]::
6536::$$$message_0048_0010_0001$$$::That's right.[lr]::
6537::$$$message_0048_0010_0002$$$::She could suffer the heroes' barbs if the man she loved would say something like that to her.[lr]::
6538::$$$message_0048_0010_0003$$$::She endured the regret of abandoning Colchis, the guilt of betraying her father, and the sin of killing her brother...[lr]::
6539::$$$message_0048_0010_0004$$$::But not once did he ever grant her the warm words she craved.::
6540::$$$message_0048_0011_0000$$$::The return voyage ended uneventfully.[lr]::
6541::$$$message_0048_0011_0001$$$::Jason would marry the princess from another land. He would return triumphantly to his homeland, Iolcus, with the Golden Fleece in hand.[lr]::
6542::$$$message_0048_0011_0002$$$::But all that awaited him was the death of his parents and a broken promise.::
6543::$$$message_0048_0012_0000$$$::"Return with the Golden Fleece, and I will recognize your kingship."[lr]::
6544::$$$message_0048_0012_0001$$$::King Pelias's promise to his son turned out to be an empty jest.[lr]::
6545::$$$message_0048_0012_0002$$$::Enraged, Jason gave his wife an order.[lr]::
6546::$$$message_0048_0012_0003$$$::   The cowardly usurper demanded: [lr]::
6547::$$$message_0048_0012_0004$$$::   "Kill King Pelias."::
6548::$$$message_0048_0013_0000$$$::While she may have been in love with Jason, Medea was still a girl.[lr]::
6549::$$$message_0048_0013_0001$$$::She was still in shock at her brother's murder by her own hand. But Jason insisted.[lr]::
6550::$$$message_0048_0013_0002$$$::Kill him.[lr]::
6551::$$$message_0048_0013_0003$$$::Kill him.[lr]::
6552::$$$message_0048_0013_0004$$$::Kill the oathbreaker. Kill Pelias.[lr]::
6553::$$$message_0048_0013_0005$$$::Kill the royal family.[lr]::
6554::$$$message_0048_0013_0006$$$::Yes, the king was not enough.[lr]::
6555::$$$message_0048_0013_0007$$$::Kill those eyesores in line for the throne, the three princesses...::
6556::$$$message_0048_0014_0000$$$::Thanks to Jason, the assassinations were prepared quickly.[lr]::
6557::$$$message_0048_0014_0001$$$::Jason invited the king and his daughters to his home.[lr]::
6558::$$$message_0048_0014_0002$$$::The witch's cauldron bubbled in the center of the chamber[line len=2][lr]::
6559::$$$message_0048_0014_0003$$$::A crystallization of the esoterica that Hecate taught her, and a basic tool of the Mystic arts.::
6560::$$$message_0048_0015_0000$$$::"Well met, my king."[lr]::
6561::$$$message_0048_0015_0001$$$::Before they knew it, the end had already begun.[lr]::
6562::$$$message_0048_0015_0002$$$::Medea couldn't resist the man she loved, nor Aphrodite's curse. She used her own magecraft to murder the king.::
6563::$$$message_0048_0016_0000$$$::"O King Pelias. Behold my wife's hidden arts."[lr]::
6564::$$$message_0048_0016_0001$$$::Beloved Jason so proudly declared.[lr]::
6565::$$$message_0048_0016_0002$$$::The girl stirred the cauldron with tearful, tired eyes.::
6566::$$$message_0048_0017_0000$$$::"This pot holds an elixir of youth.[lr]::
6567::$$$message_0048_0017_0001$$$::My wife _____ is skilled at such magecraft."[lr]::
6568::$$$message_0048_0017_0002$$$::That's what he said. The man she suddenly fell in love with, one day.[lr]::
6569::$$$message_0048_0017_0003$$$::She continued the spell, unable to resist.::
6570::$$$message_0048_0018_0000$$$::Her hands felt as heavy as lead.[lr]::
6571::$$$message_0048_0018_0001$$$::...Had she ever gotten a chance to rest once she left her home?[lr]::
6572::$$$message_0048_0018_0002$$$::Her mind and body were utterly exhausted. It was like she was lost in a fog.[lr]::
6573::$$$message_0048_0018_0003$$$::She would forget this fatigue.[lr]::
6574::$$$message_0048_0018_0004$$$::This sadness would fade.[lr]::
6575::$$$message_0048_0018_0005$$$::...Ah.[lr]::
6576::$$$message_0048_0018_0006$$$::Was this really what she learned magecraft for...?::
6577::$$$message_0048_0019_0000$$$::She chopped up an old sheep and put it in the cauldron.[lr]::
6578::$$$message_0048_0019_0001$$$::It swirled and bubbled until it melted into the pot.[lr]::
6579::$$$message_0048_0019_0002$$$::Then, Medea resurrected the butchered animal.[lr]::
6580::$$$message_0048_0019_0003$$$::It emerged with glossy skin and lively eyes.[lr]::
6581::$$$message_0048_0019_0004$$$::The once mature sheep was now a young lamb.::
6582::$$$message_0048_0020_0000$$$::Stunned, the king asked that he be revitalized as well.[lr]::
6583::$$$message_0048_0020_0001$$$::The girl replied,[lr]::
6584::$$$message_0048_0020_0002$$$::just as her love told her to.[lr]::
6585::$$$message_0048_0020_0003$$$::"To do that, we must first cut up your entire body. The subject of this spell must die first."[lr]::
6586::$$$message_0048_0020_0004$$$::Fearlessly, the king ordered his three beloved daughters to do the deed.[lr]::
6587::$$$message_0048_0020_0005$$$::The three princesses butchered the king...[lr]::
6588::$$$message_0048_0020_0006$$$::...and dropped his parts into the cauldron.::
6589::$$$message_0048_0021_0000$$$::"Do you see that!? What horrible daughters! They slaughtered their own father!"[lr]::
6590::$$$message_0048_0021_0001$$$::The king did not come back to life.[lr]::
6591::$$$message_0048_0021_0002$$$::The princesses wailed.[lr]::
6592::$$$message_0048_0021_0003$$$::Medea's love tied up the women.::
6593::$$$message_0048_0022_0000$$$::"Patricide! The gods will never forgive this![lr]::
6594::$$$message_0048_0022_0001$$$::Daughters of Pelias, you will pay with your lives...!"[lr]::
6595::$$$message_0048_0022_0002$$$::Pelias's daughters wailed.[lr]::
6596::$$$message_0048_0022_0003$$$::"How did this happen?" they screamed.[lr]::
6597::$$$message_0048_0022_0004$$$::They begged for forgiveness, not from the gods, but from their dead father.[lr]::
6598::$$$message_0048_0022_0005$$$::But this man, Jason, did not forgive them.::
6599::$$$message_0048_0023_0000$$$::At that moment, Aphrodite's curse disappeared.[lr]::
6600::$$$message_0048_0023_0001$$$::It was as if a cloud lifted from Medea's heart.[lr]::
6601::$$$message_0048_0023_0002$$$::But it was all too late.[lr]::
6602::$$$message_0048_0023_0003$$$::She betrayed her country and killed her brother.[lr]::
6603::$$$message_0048_0023_0004$$$::She then assassinated a king and watched three innocent princesses die.[lr]::
6604::$$$message_0048_0023_0005$$$::That was the day.[lr]::
6605::$$$message_0048_0023_0006$$$::That day, the girl matured into a true witch.::
6606::$$$message_0048_0024_0000$$$::Jason's glory on the throne was brief.[lr]::
6607::$$$message_0048_0024_0001$$$::Once the citizens learned of their king's murder, Jason and the foreign witch were driven from Iolcus.[lr]::
6608::$$$message_0048_0024_0002$$$::Without a home, Jason and the witch wandered Greece until they arrived in Corinth.::
6609::$$$message_0048_0025_0000$$$::The king of Corinth welcomed Jason and offered his daughter Graeae's hand in marriage.[lr]::
6610::$$$message_0048_0025_0001$$$::Would he marry Graeae and seize the Corinthian throne?[lr]::
6611::$$$message_0048_0025_0002$$$::Would he accept the king of Corinth's blessing, even while married to a witch?[lr]::
6612::$$$message_0048_0025_0003$$$::The choice was clear to Jason.[lr]::
6613::$$$message_0048_0025_0004$$$::He already had two children with the witch, but such bonds could not keep Jason from moving on.::
6614::$$$message_0048_0026_0000$$$::Jason abandoned the witch and ran to Graeae's side.[lr]::
6615::$$$message_0048_0026_0001$$$::"Please don't go." "Please don't go."[lr]::
6616::$$$message_0048_0026_0002$$$::"I abandoned my country for you." "I threw everything away for your sake."[lr]::
6617::$$$message_0048_0026_0003$$$::"Have pity on me, on our children."[lr]::
6618::$$$message_0048_0026_0004$$$::The witch wept at her husband.::
6619::$$$message_0048_0027_0000$$$::"That's all you have to say? It's your own fault I lost my homeland, foul foreign witch. Never once have I loved you."[lr]::
6620::$$$message_0048_0027_0001$$$::"Ahh...aaaahhh, hah..."[lr]::
6621::$$$message_0048_0027_0002$$$::...Her homeland was so far away now.[lr]::
6622::$$$message_0048_0027_0003$$$::She stepped on foreign soil without wishing for anything.::
6623::$$$message_0048_0028_0000$$$::And then...[lr]::
6624::$$$message_0048_0028_0001$$$::After a long journey, a wish was finally born in her heart.[lr]::
6625::$$$message_0048_0028_0002$$$::How to make it come true, though?[lr]::
6626::$$$message_0048_0028_0003$$$::Everything seemed like a bad dream.[lr]::
6627::$$$message_0048_0028_0004$$$::The girl had morphed into a hideous witch. Even if she went home, no one would believe she was that childish princess.[lr]::
6628::$$$message_0048_0028_0005$$$::...She had changed far too much.[lr]::
6629::$$$message_0048_0028_0006$$$::The castle she was raised in should still be wreathed in green, like before.::
6630::$$$message_0048_0029_0000$$$::On the day of Jason's wedding...[lr]::
6631::$$$message_0048_0029_0001$$$::Amidst the nationwide festival everyone celebrated, Corinth perished.[lr]::
6632::$$$message_0048_0029_0002$$$::Graeae died in a fire, and the hero who expected to become a king became an outcast once again.::
6633::$$$message_0048_0030_0000$$$::Myth and legend do not record the rest of their tale.[lr]::
6634::$$$message_0048_0030_0001$$$::The young man who once led heroes aboard the Argo fell asleep beneath its rotting mast. It fell, crushing him to death.[lr]::
6635::$$$message_0048_0030_0002$$$::As for the girl he took from her country, she must have continued to wander Greece as a witch.::
6636::$$$message_0048_0031_0000$$$::Even now, she stares out into the distance from those gray shores...[lr]::
6637::$$$message_0048_0031_0001$$$::...remembering sin upon sin...[lr]::
6638::$$$message_0048_0031_0002$$$::...and dream upon abandoned dream.[lr]::
6639::$$$message_0048_0031_0003$$$::Though she knows her dream is lost...[lr]::
6640::$$$message_0048_0031_0004$$$::...her thoughts remain on it, in penance. ::
6641::$$$message_0048_0032_0000$$$::                                     I feel dizzy.[lr]::
6642::$$$message_0048_0032_0001$$$::                                     I must have been half-daydreaming.::
6643::$$$message_0048_0033_0000$$$::"...Oh, right. I was going to ask her something."[lr]::
6644::$$$message_0048_0033_0001$$$::I'll be fine. She'll talk to me, at least.[lr]::
6645::$$$message_0048_0033_0002$$$::Curiosity might be leading me to the lion's den, but thankfully, the big cat is full right now.[lr]::
6646::$$$message_0048_0033_0003$$$::I bet she'll let even annoying questions slide if they alleviate her boredom.::
6647::$$$message_0048_0034_0000$$$::"You're back? I don't know what you're plotting, but you're brave, I'll admit.[lr]::
6648::$$$message_0048_0034_0001$$$::You should know how dangerous I am when I'm alone."::
6649::$$$message_0048_0035_0000$$$::She's exactly right. Nothing could be riskier than approaching Caster when no one else is around.[lr]::
6650::$$$message_0048_0035_0001$$$::Not because she can use her magecraft without worrying about witnesses, but because she can't control her emotions when no one else is watching.::
6651::$$$message_0048_0036_0000$$$::If Caster loses her temper, there won't be any stopping her.[lr]::
6652::$$$message_0048_0036_0001$$$::She'd play the cold witch if someone else was watching, but she might get hysterical if we're alone.[lr]::
6653::$$$message_0048_0036_0002$$$::Still, though...[lr]::
6654::$$$message_0048_0036_0003$$$::Everyone's got things that make them a little unstable or prone to fantasizing.::
6655::$$$message_0048_0037_0000$$$::"I was just curious about something.[lr]::
6656::$$$message_0048_0037_0001$$$::You seem like you're in a good mood right now, so I thought I'd ask you about it."[lr]::
6657::$$$message_0048_0037_0002$$$::The air grows faintly suffocating.[lr]::
6658::$$$message_0048_0037_0003$$$::She must have deduced what I'm about to ask.::
6659::$$$message_0048_0038_0000$$$::"And what would that be? I doubt it's anything pleasant."::
6660::$$$message_0048_0039_0000$$$::"Just a question. I'll be brief, since I'm afraid to stay too long. I know you don't intend on fixing this situation. I won't press the issue.[lr]::
6661::$$$message_0048_0039_0001$$$::But there is something else I want to know.[lr]::
6662::$$$message_0048_0039_0002$$$::A mage of your caliber should be able to investigate this four-day loop easily. Does that mean you know what's [font italic=true]really[font italic=false] happening?"::
6663::$$$message_0048_0040_0000$$$::"What an interesting thought.[lr]::
6664::$$$message_0048_0040_0001$$$::You think I understand this entire mechanism?"[lr]::
6665::$$$message_0048_0040_0002$$$::She smirks.[lr]::
6666::$$$message_0048_0040_0003$$$::Unlike her earlier smile, it's an expression that spells my doom.::
6667::$$$message_0048_0041_0000$$$::"...Heh heh. Unfortunately, you're wrong, boy.[lr]::
6668::$$$message_0048_0041_0001$$$::It's true that early on, I went to great lengths to investigate and very nearly gleaned the truth. But now, I'm still one step away from it.[lr]::
6669::$$$message_0048_0041_0002$$$::After all, a game ceases to be fun once you know everything about it, right? That's why I stopped pursuing the matter and let it be."::
6670::$$$message_0048_0042_0000$$$::"...Huh. So you stopped trying.[lr]::
6671::$$$message_0048_0042_0001$$$::Isn't that pretty much the same, though? You know almost everything."[lr]::
6672::$$$message_0048_0042_0002$$$::"Yes. But I haven't told anyone.[lr]::
6673::$$$message_0048_0042_0003$$$::The case would end once the culprit was identified. But that culprit is powerless, and I have no obligation to catch them."::
6674::$$$message_0048_0043_0000$$$::"I see. You're just spectating since no one is getting hurt... That's awfully passive of you.[lr]::
6675::$$$message_0048_0043_0001$$$::So are you just going to keep watching from the sidelines?"[lr]::
6676::$$$message_0048_0043_0002$$$::"...I believe I already stated my intentions.[lr]::
6677::$$$message_0048_0043_0003$$$::But that could change, in the last moment.[lr]::
6678::$$$message_0048_0043_0004$$$::If this is going to end, then I won't sit idly by... [cacheimage storage=キャスターローブ無し02d(中)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=200 storage=キャスターローブ無し02d(中)]I mean my Master, of course, not me."::
6679::$$$message_0048_0044_0000$$$::Caster sighs, muttering that there isn't a difference.[lr]::
6680::$$$message_0048_0044_0001$$$::Legends call her a treacherous witch, but Caster is utterly obedient to her Master, Souichirou Kuzuki.::
6681::$$$message_0048_0045_0000$$$::...You could also call her head-over-heels in love.[lr]::
6682::$$$message_0048_0045_0001$$$::It's obvious to anyone besides Kuzuki and Caster.[lr]::
6683::$$$message_0048_0045_0002$$$::If her beloved Souichirou asks Caster to help him with something, she'll do it, no matter what.::
6684::$$$message_0048_0046_0000$$$::"...[lr]::
6685::$$$message_0048_0046_0001$$$::...I know you want this to keep going. But if Mr. Kuzuki asks you to solve the loop, will you help me?"::
6686::$$$message_0048_0047_0000$$$::"Yes. I won't obstruct the culprit behind it, but I won't help them either.[lr]::
6687::$$$message_0048_0047_0001$$$::In fact, I can't. I can't change whether it ends or not."::
6688::$$$message_0048_0048_0000$$$::"Understand me? That's why you're an eyesore. If you want this to go on, you should just let it, but you're trying to stop it.[lr]::
6689::$$$message_0048_0048_0001$$$::...Honestly, I've considered killing you a few times."::
6690::$$$message_0048_0049_0000$$$::"...Oof. That was a joke, I hope."[lr]::
6691::$$$message_0048_0049_0001$$$::"Was it, now? You know whether I'm the type of person to jest."[lr]::
6692::$$$message_0048_0049_0002$$$::"..."[lr]::
6693::$$$message_0048_0049_0003$$$::Chills run down my spine.[lr]::
6694::$$$message_0048_0049_0004$$$::I really shouldn't overstay my welcome.::
6695::$$$message_0048_0050_0000$$$::"...Whew. Okay, I understand you're only going to spectate. I'll try not to bring this up again...but, uh, why haven't you killed me yet? You could've tried at least once."[lr]::
6696::$$$message_0048_0050_0001$$$::I'd prefer it if she didn't, though.[lr]::
6697::$$$message_0048_0050_0002$$$::Knowing Caster, I'd expect her to give into temptation and skewer me at least once.::
6698::$$$message_0048_0051_0000$$$::"What a silly question.[lr]::
6699::$$$message_0048_0051_0001$$$::Because my Master hasn't asked me to, of course."[lr]::
6700::$$$message_0048_0051_0002$$$::She answers clearly.[lr]::
6701::$$$message_0048_0051_0003$$$::I narrow my eyes at that sense of purity.::
6702::$$$message_0048_0052_0000$$$::"Right. Yeah, that adds up.[lr]::
6703::$$$message_0048_0052_0001$$$::...One last question, then.[lr]::
6704::$$$message_0048_0052_0002$$$::Just for conversation's sake, what do you think Souichirou Kuzuki would do if he found out what's happening? Do you think he'd try to fix it, or leave it alone?[lr]::
6705::$$$message_0048_0052_0003$$$::...C'mon. How do you two [font italic=true]really[font italic=false] feel about all this?"::
6706::$$$message_0048_0053_0000$$$::For a moment, the air freezes over.[lr]::
6707::$$$message_0048_0053_0001$$$::I could've died four times in those three seconds.[lr]::
6708::$$$message_0048_0053_0002$$$::Caster's gaze alone contains a lethal amount of magical energy...::
6709::$$$message_0048_0054_0000$$$::"...He would resolve it.[lr]::
6710::$$$message_0048_0054_0001$$$::Souichirou's morals are different from yours, boy, but he's a man who will correct himself if he feels that he is wrong."[lr]::
6711::$$$message_0048_0054_0002$$$::...but she answers the question with a hint of sadness behind her words.::
6712::$$$message_0048_0055_0000$$$::"Oh. So your Master's like me,"[lr]::
6713::$$$message_0048_0055_0001$$$::I murmur reverently, as I let the gloom out of my lungs.::
6714::$$$message_0048_0056_0000$$$::"No. You resemble my Master."[lr]::
6715::$$$message_0048_0056_0001$$$::I hear a ring of pride in her voice.::
6716::$$$message_0048_0057_0000$$$::"Yeah. Well, I'll leave it at that.[lr]::
6717::$$$message_0048_0057_0001$$$::Sorry for the boring conversation. You just keep on doing what you're doing."::
6718::$$$message_0048_0058_0000$$$::"I don't need you to tell me that.[lr]::
6719::$$$message_0048_0058_0001$$$::Although...out of respect for your lone efforts, when the end comes, I'll come send you off."[lr]::
6720::$$$message_0048_0058_0002$$$::"..."[lr]::
6721::$$$message_0048_0058_0003$$$::I'm shocked.[lr]::
6722::$$$message_0048_0058_0004$$$::I fail to keep my jaw from dropping.::
6723::$$$message_0048_0059_0000$$$::"What are you looking at me like that for? Do you understand what I said? I won't do anything until the very end."[lr]::
6724::$$$message_0048_0059_0001$$$::"I know. But you still said you'll help me.[lr]::
6725::$$$message_0048_0059_0002$$$::[chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=キャスターローブ無し02b(中)]...I'm grateful to be able to depend on you.[lr]::
6726::$$$message_0048_0059_0003$$$::Your help might be the biggest encouragement I could ask for."::
6727::$$$message_0048_0060_0000$$$::I leave Caster's garden.[lr]::
6728::$$$message_0048_0060_0001$$$::She puts her robe back on and watches me go.[lr]::
6729::$$$message_0048_0060_0002$$$::That was uncomfortable.[lr]::
6730::$$$message_0048_0060_0003$$$::I felt so bright and pleasant just now,[lr]::
6731::$$$message_0048_0060_0004$$$::but for a moment, I glimpsed her sinister past.::
6732::$$$message_0048_0061_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"How do you two really feel about all this?"[font italic=false]::
6733::$$$message_0048_0062_0000$$$::The boy who said that leaves,[lr]::
6734::$$$message_0048_0062_0001$$$::while the witch lingers, wrapping herself in her dark cloak.::
6735::$$$message_0048_0063_0000$$$::One resembles the other.[lr]::
6736::$$$message_0048_0063_0001$$$::They seem the same.[lr]::
6737::$$$message_0048_0063_0002$$$::                                          [font italic=true]"Oh. So your Master's like me..."[font italic=false][lr]::
6738::$$$message_0048_0063_0003$$$::The present mimics reality.[lr]::
6739::$$$message_0048_0063_0004$$$::Reality and illusion seem the same.[lr]::
6740::$$$message_0048_0063_0005$$$::                                          [font italic=true]"No. You resemble my Master..."[font italic=false][lr]::
6741::$$$message_0048_0063_0006$$$::Without anything to focus on, her thoughts swirl, blending into one another.::
6742::$$$message_0048_0064_0000$$$::[font italic=true]Melt, melt. Bubble, bubble.[font italic=false][lr]::
6743::$$$message_0048_0064_0001$$$::The images of this world, and the past, feel like someone else's memories entirely.[lr]::
6744::$$$message_0048_0064_0002$$$::Her memories when she was a living mortal,[lr]::
6745::$$$message_0048_0064_0003$$$::and the bad dream she just had moments earlier.[lr]::
6746::$$$message_0048_0064_0004$$$::The dead mixes with the living, like the mutton in the cauldron.::
6747::$$$message_0048_0065_0000$$$::"You want the truth?"[lr]::
6748::$$$message_0048_0065_0001$$$::The witch bites her lip, feeling horrid.[lr]::
6749::$$$message_0048_0065_0002$$$::Is this an evening shower?[lr]::
6750::$$$message_0048_0065_0003$$$::She hears thunder in the distance.[lr]::
6751::$$$message_0048_0065_0004$$$::The pitter-patter of rain in the trees reminds her of the day they met.[lr]::
6752::$$$message_0048_0065_0005$$$::...When the frustration overtakes her like this, it's the only memory that comes to mind.[lr]::
6753::$$$message_0048_0065_0006$$$::   That day.[lr]::
6754::$$$message_0048_0065_0007$$$::His dry hand, grasping the hand of a foolish woman whom nobody wanted.::
6755::$$$message_0048_0066_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"Rain. It's raining..."[font italic=false][lr]::
6756::$$$message_0048_0066_0001$$$::She noticed her hands were bloody.[lr]::
6757::$$$message_0048_0066_0002$$$::She could hear how ragged her breathing was.[lr]::
6758::$$$message_0048_0066_0003$$$::The chill was creeping into her body, and her mind was so blank it scared her.::
6759::$$$message_0048_0067_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"Rain...? I-it's rain."[font italic=false][lr]::
6760::$$$message_0048_0067_0001$$$::Her body was about to disappear. Her mind was nearly lost.[lr]::
6761::$$$message_0048_0067_0002$$$::The sky above was distant. She could call for help, but nobody would come. She couldn't stop the heat from leaving her body.::
6762::$$$message_0048_0068_0000$$$::"Ahh... But this night is...different."[lr]::
6763::$$$message_0048_0068_0001$$$::Her magical energy was practically spent.[lr]::
6764::$$$message_0048_0068_0002$$$::Only the slightest of spells was still available to her. She had no way to stop her life from fading.[lr]::
6765::$$$message_0048_0068_0003$$$::No, to begin with...[lr]::
6766::$$$message_0048_0068_0004$$$::[font italic=true]"The rain felt cold because that night was warmer, and brighter..."[font italic=false][lr]::
6767::$$$message_0048_0068_0005$$$::He died nearly instantly.::
6768::$$$message_0048_0069_0000$$$::Let us speak of a certain man.[lr]::
6769::$$$message_0048_0069_0001$$$::Approximately twenty-five years ago...[lr]::
6770::$$$message_0048_0069_0002$$$::There was a "weapon" who had been honed for nearly as long as he lived.::
6771::$$$message_0048_0070_0000$$$::He never did find out exactly who [font italic=true]they[font italic=false] were.[lr]::
6772::$$$message_0048_0070_0001$$$::In a remote mountain village, he came into being among a community of ascetics.[lr]::
6773::$$$message_0048_0070_0002$$$::He was a baby with no ties, no parents or siblings. Thus, it would not be quite accurate to say that he was "born."::
6774::$$$message_0048_0071_0000$$$::The baby was raised by the group.[lr]::
6775::$$$message_0048_0071_0001$$$::He was blessedly innocent.[lr]::
6776::$$$message_0048_0071_0002$$$::He knew nothing of the outside world, and accepted his lot in life.[lr]::
6777::$$$message_0048_0071_0003$$$::Never mind that it was no place for a person to live,[lr]::
6778::$$$message_0048_0071_0004$$$::nor did it contain many means by which one may survive.[lr]::
6779::$$$message_0048_0071_0005$$$::He lived there for twenty years.[lr]::
6780::$$$message_0048_0071_0006$$$::He spent that time training a single art, never leaving the ten square meter home he was given in the forest.::
6781::$$$message_0048_0072_0000$$$::When he was ten years old, he learned that the group was a sort of factory,[lr]::
6782::$$$message_0048_0072_0001$$$::a place where people mass-produced living necessities.[lr]::
6783::$$$message_0048_0072_0002$$$::He had no experience making things, so he didn't need to think about what he would do.::
6784::$$$message_0048_0073_0000$$$::He had no objection to being a living necessity himself. If anything, it set him at ease.[lr]::
6785::$$$message_0048_0073_0001$$$::It would be strange to think otherwise.[lr]::
6786::$$$message_0048_0073_0002$$$::Day after day, he repeated the same movement.[lr]::
6787::$$$message_0048_0073_0003$$$::The ______ told him to perfect this single movement. There was no need to be versatile.[lr]::
6788::$$$message_0048_0073_0004$$$::Just like a tool.[lr]::
6789::$$$message_0048_0073_0005$$$::They accepted that they would be used as tools for people they did not know, and worked to refine their utility.::
6790::$$$message_0048_0074_0000$$$::Conversely...[lr]::
6791::$$$message_0048_0074_0001$$$::Those who couldn't accept it mentally broke down. They couldn't keep up with the daily routine and disappeared, leaving no trace even from the other tools' memories.::
6792::$$$message_0048_0075_0000$$$::Soon after that, he realized what his "purpose" was.[lr]::
6793::$$$message_0048_0075_0001$$$::They taught him other things in preparation for a certain eventuality.[lr]::
6794::$$$message_0048_0075_0002$$$::They were to serve as living necessities for humans, but they needed to be able to mimic humans in order to exercise their purpose.[lr]::
6795::$$$message_0048_0075_0003$$$::They learned the necessary knowledge to function as humans.[lr]::
6796::$$$message_0048_0075_0004$$$::It was excessive, but without it, they wouldn't have much chance to exercise their purpose.[lr]::
6797::$$$message_0048_0075_0005$$$::The ______ seemed reluctant to impart excess functions, but it was unavoidable.[lr]::
6798::$$$message_0048_0075_0006$$$::It must have been a bitter decision for them.::
6799::$$$message_0048_0076_0000$$$::He gained knowledge he'd never been taught before.[lr]::
6800::$$$message_0048_0076_0001$$$::The common wisdom needed to be an incoherent human being was little more than dead weight slowing him down.[lr]::
6801::$$$message_0048_0076_0002$$$::Still, that knowledge finally allowed him to give a name to his purpose: [lr]::
6802::$$$message_0048_0076_0003$$$::                                                              murder.[rf][lr]::
6803::$$$message_0048_0076_0004$$$::What they desired of him was the ability to end a life without anyone else knowing or finding out.::
6804::$$$message_0048_0077_0000$$$::He was a fast learner. He was often called away from his ten square meter home to serve at the ______'s tomb.[lr]::
6805::$$$message_0048_0077_0001$$$::Still, it only happened about once a month.[lr]::
6806::$$$message_0048_0077_0002$$$::There, he was provided with the funds to perfect himself,[lr]::
6807::$$$message_0048_0077_0003$$$::and he learned what the ______ who used him looked like.::
6808::$$$message_0048_0078_0000$$$::The tomb was a pristine space.[lr]::
6809::$$$message_0048_0078_0001$$$::There were all sorts of rumors about the building. Some said it was a hellish, horrifying place, while others whispered of a nest of oni. But it was a stark, spotless, white world.[lr]::
6810::$$$message_0048_0078_0002$$$::There were no tools discarded and vivisected for disobeying a _____,[lr]::
6811::$$$message_0048_0078_0003$$$::no traces of being punished for dishonoring a _____ by having one's brain removed and transplanted into an animal,[lr]::
6812::$$$message_0048_0078_0004$$$::no tank packed with the flesh of children was brought in to give a _____ comfort.[lr]::
6813::$$$message_0048_0078_0005$$$::No such things were there.::
6814::$$$message_0048_0079_0000$$$::Those things definitely happened, but not there.[lr]::
6815::$$$message_0048_0079_0001$$$::In this pristine space, the ______,[lr]::
6816::$$$message_0048_0079_0002$$$::without feeling a speck of guilt,[lr]::
6817::$$$message_0048_0079_0003$$$::to relieve their boredom, though not quite successfully,[lr]::
6818::$$$message_0048_0079_0004$$$::would exchange unrelated, ordinary humans for money,[lr]::
6819::$$$message_0048_0079_0005$$$::only to increase the number of dishes on tonight's menu, if only by one bite.::
6820::$$$message_0048_0080_0000$$$::    Please help me.[lr]::
6821::$$$message_0048_0080_0001$$$::I don't want to die. Please let me go. They stifled their filthy cries while laughing.::
6822::$$$message_0048_0081_0000$$$::In their final moments, those being harvested would realize something, although the ______ weren't even aware of it.[lr]::
6823::$$$message_0048_0081_0001$$$::These "humans" speak a different language from us. We're the same species, but our minds are built differently.[lr]::
6824::$$$message_0048_0081_0002$$$::Just as humans can't hear the voices of the food on a dining table,[lr]::
6825::$$$message_0048_0081_0003$$$::the ______ would never hear the voices of humans other than themselves.::
6826::$$$message_0048_0082_0000$$$::That applied outside of the tomb, too.[lr]::
6827::$$$message_0048_0082_0001$$$::The one in charge of him once said that there were only a few people[lr]::
6828::$$$message_0048_0082_0002$$$::with the privilege to use us tools.[lr]::
6829::$$$message_0048_0082_0003$$$::                       That this world was ruled by humans who weren't human.[rf][lr]::
6830::$$$message_0048_0082_0004$$$::He was taught that his purpose was to kill a single person for their benefit.::
6831::$$$message_0048_0083_0000$$$::He didn't consider it evil.[lr]::
6832::$$$message_0048_0083_0001$$$::Mentally, he was already complete.[lr]::
6833::$$$message_0048_0083_0002$$$::He was raised with values that served the ______'s needs.[lr]::
6834::$$$message_0048_0083_0003$$$::To him, murder wasn't evil.[lr]::
6835::$$$message_0048_0083_0004$$$::Only things that didn't follow logic were evil.[lr]::
6836::$$$message_0048_0083_0005$$$::His logic as a tool.[lr]::
6837::$$$message_0048_0083_0006$$$::The logic of his existence.[lr]::
6838::$$$message_0048_0083_0007$$$::Simply put, a pen that couldn't write was evil, and a tool made to kill people was flawed if its target escaped death.::
6839::$$$message_0048_0084_0000$$$::By that theory, the _____ weren't wrong at all.[lr]::
6840::$$$message_0048_0084_0001$$$::They were creatures granted such privilege and preferences.[lr]::
6841::$$$message_0048_0084_0002$$$::They ruled the world, so it didn't make sense for them to care about their slaves.[lr]::
6842::$$$message_0048_0084_0003$$$::That's what he was taught. Even faced with the ______'s injustice, he never once despised them.::
6843::$$$message_0048_0085_0000$$$::If there was one bad thing in his life...[lr]::
6844::$$$message_0048_0085_0001$$$::...it was that he was never to question his purpose.[lr]::
6845::$$$message_0048_0085_0002$$$::By his values, that was correct. But he still wondered.[lr]::
6846::$$$message_0048_0085_0003$$$::What if he had been assigned a different purpose?[lr]::
6847::$$$message_0048_0085_0004$$$::What sort of tool would he have been shaped into? Such thoughts were nothing but evil, but still he had them.::
6848::$$$message_0048_0086_0000$$$::He continued living for his purpose.[lr]::
6849::$$$message_0048_0086_0001$$$::They taught him the art of using his arms in a way they called "Snake," but he'd perfected that years ago.[lr]::
6850::$$$message_0048_0086_0002$$$::Still, his life didn't change.[lr]::
6851::$$$message_0048_0086_0003$$$::He wasn't taught any new techniques.[lr]::
6852::$$$message_0048_0086_0004$$$::He was only created to utilize Snake. Even if he had the capacity to learn more, there was no point in adding other functions.[lr]::
6853::$$$message_0048_0086_0005$$$::Another ten years passed. By then, it had been twenty years.[lr]::
6854::$$$message_0048_0086_0006$$$::His usefulness as a tool would expire soon. Finally, he was given a chance to carry out his purpose.::
6855::$$$message_0048_0087_0000$$$::"Your upbringing and completion cost twenty million, in both time and money."[lr]::
6856::$$$message_0048_0087_0001$$$::That was one difference between them and other organizations.[lr]::
6857::$$$message_0048_0087_0002$$$::Whatever their function, the tools were strictly limited to a single kill.[lr]::
6858::$$$message_0048_0087_0003$$$::Whether they turned out to be brilliant talents or mediocre trash, they all shared the same end.::
6859::$$$message_0048_0088_0000$$$::"A tool worth twenty million should complete work equal to that amount."[lr]::
6860::$$$message_0048_0088_0001$$$::You will break even. You will not be used again. Once you complete your task, kill yourself.[lr]::
6861::$$$message_0048_0088_0002$$$::Those were their absolute rules.[lr]::
6862::$$$message_0048_0088_0003$$$::They would be ordered to kill someone using arts beyond human comprehension, honed over decades, and then end themselves once the task was complete.::
6863::$$$message_0048_0089_0000$$$::He obeyed that doctrine.[lr]::
6864::$$$message_0048_0089_0001$$$::His target was said to be behind several layers of security.[lr]::
6865::$$$message_0048_0089_0002$$$::The ______ would provide a social position for him to discreetly make contact.[lr]::
6866::$$$message_0048_0089_0003$$$::After that, he just had to do the deed.[lr]::
6867::$$$message_0048_0089_0004$$$::His work required no weapons, which made it easy to approach the mark.::
6868::$$$message_0048_0090_0000$$$::The tools' deaths were assured the moment they left their homes in the forest.[lr]::
6869::$$$message_0048_0090_0001$$$::It was to be a one-way trip, with no option to agree or refuse.[lr]::
6870::$$$message_0048_0090_0002$$$::As for happiness...if he was being honest, there was a hint of it.[lr]::
6871::$$$message_0048_0090_0003$$$::He'd lived a twenty-year calculation.[lr]::
6872::$$$message_0048_0090_0004$$$::How impressive would his purpose turn out to be?[lr]::
6873::$$$message_0048_0090_0005$$$::Even if only death awaited him, it was enough to look forward to seeing it.::
6874::$$$message_0048_0091_0000$$$::The task was disappointingly trivial.[lr]::
6875::$$$message_0048_0091_0001$$$::The expected security was no trouble at all.[lr]::
6876::$$$message_0048_0091_0002$$$::He ended up finishing the job early when he visited the building to perform reconnaissance before the strike.::
6877::$$$message_0048_0092_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
6878::$$$message_0048_0092_0001$$$::How to articulate his emotions in that moment?[lr]::
6879::$$$message_0048_0092_0002$$$::The immediate feeling in his chest...was a [font italic=true]void.[font italic=false][lr]::
6880::$$$message_0048_0092_0003$$$::He felt neither delight nor sadness.[lr]::
6881::$$$message_0048_0092_0004$$$::He felt neither revulsion nor joy.[lr]::
6882::$$$message_0048_0092_0005$$$::If there was anything...[lr]::
6883::$$$message_0048_0092_0006$$$::It's that he thought he would feel something when his purpose was fulfilled, but it created no ripples in his heart.::
6884::$$$message_0048_0093_0000$$$::What if...[lr]::
6885::$$$message_0048_0093_0001$$$::What if, at that moment, he [font italic=true]had[font italic=false] felt something? Would he have become someone else?[lr]::
6886::$$$message_0048_0093_0002$$$::If he had felt joy, he would have killed himself.[lr]::
6887::$$$message_0048_0093_0003$$$::If he had felt sadness, he might have gone on to become a genuine serial killer.::
6888::$$$message_0048_0094_0000$$$::But there was nothing.[lr]::
6889::$$$message_0048_0094_0001$$$::He really felt nothing at the result of his twenty years of training.::
6890::$$$message_0048_0095_0000$$$::The sensation of killing his target was neither pleasant nor unpleasant.[lr]::
6891::$$$message_0048_0095_0001$$$::All he felt was his palm, breaking the target's neck bone like a wooden doll.[lr]::
6892::$$$message_0048_0095_0002$$$::No compensation.[lr]::
6893::$$$message_0048_0095_0003$$$::No reward.[lr]::
6894::$$$message_0048_0095_0004$$$::The impact of taking a life wasn't there.::
6895::$$$message_0048_0096_0000$$$::The purpose he knew was itself strange.[lr]::
6896::$$$message_0048_0096_0001$$$::He didn't want it.[lr]::
6897::$$$message_0048_0096_0002$$$::He didn't need it.[lr]::
6898::$$$message_0048_0096_0003$$$::No technique was required to kill his target.[lr]::
6899::$$$message_0048_0096_0004$$$::The murder was virtually an accident.[lr]::
6900::$$$message_0048_0096_0005$$$::It was an assassination a child could have carried out, much less a trained killer.[lr]::
6901::$$$message_0048_0096_0006$$$::    It all felt so unnecessary.::
6902::$$$message_0048_0097_0000$$$::What were the twenty years of training needed for?[lr]::
6903::$$$message_0048_0097_0001$$$::His purpose left nothing behind.[lr]::
6904::$$$message_0048_0097_0002$$$::His experiences were pointless.::
6905::$$$message_0048_0098_0000$$$::It shouldn't have created any doubts.[lr]::
6906::$$$message_0048_0098_0001$$$::He was sure there was no reason. No reason for anything.[lr]::
6907::$$$message_0048_0098_0002$$$::All he knew about this corpse was its name. Then, he realized something about his usual, emotionless self: [lr]::
6908::$$$message_0048_0098_0003$$$::"...I'm thirsty,"[lr]::
6909::$$$message_0048_0098_0004$$$::he concluded, and with that, settled his own account.::
6910::$$$message_0048_0099_0000$$$::He did not kill himself. He became a person who left the group.[lr]::
6911::$$$message_0048_0099_0001$$$::He didn't even consider going into hiding.[lr]::
6912::$$$message_0048_0099_0002$$$::He used the social position he was given for his purpose to move to a distant town without arousing any suspicion.[lr]::
6913::$$$message_0048_0099_0003$$$::He was provided with a teacher's personality, but he somehow learned the skills and knowledge needed to fulfill the role.::
6914::$$$message_0048_0100_0000$$$::It was a life unlike any he'd lived. There were no hindrances preventing him from carrying out his new role.[lr]::
6915::$$$message_0048_0100_0001$$$::But he did feel a small bit of confusion.[lr]::
6916::$$$message_0048_0100_0002$$$::It was like a foreign object lodged in his chest.[lr]::
6917::$$$message_0048_0100_0003$$$::In the end, he never did understand what exactly this sense of unease was.::
6918::$$$message_0048_0101_0000$$$::His life as a teacher, projected to last six months, went on for five years.[lr]::
6919::$$$message_0048_0101_0001$$$::No one came looking for him, so he'd decided to live without worrying about pursuers.[lr]::
6920::$$$message_0048_0101_0002$$$::He didn't yearn for a normal life.[lr]::
6921::$$$message_0048_0101_0003$$$::For nearly twenty years, all he'd done was train in the art of killing.[lr]::
6922::$$$message_0048_0101_0004$$$::He made up his mind: if this was all he had to show for it, then he would simply disappear without accomplishing anything.::
6923::$$$message_0048_0102_0000$$$::One could say...[lr]::
6924::$$$message_0048_0102_0001$$$::...that he lost his opportunity to find happiness in life.[lr]::
6925::$$$message_0048_0102_0002$$$::People spend the rest of their lives trying to fulfill the wishes they develop prior to maturity.[lr]::
6926::$$$message_0048_0102_0003$$$::Regardless of whether they succeed or not, it's a drug that consumes the painful time they spend trying.::
6927::$$$message_0048_0103_0000$$$::He lacked such motivation, so all he could do was pass the time aimlessly.[lr]::
6928::$$$message_0048_0103_0001$$$::He had neither ideals nor delusions.[lr]::
6929::$$$message_0048_0103_0002$$$::He resolved that his next obligation would be to live until his body failed, until he no longer functioned as a tool.::
6930::$$$message_0048_0104_0000$$$::It may have sounded robotic of him, but he was a human, no different from those around him.[lr]::
6931::$$$message_0048_0104_0001$$$::The only difference was that his ability to be emotionally moved was long dead,::
6932::$$$message_0048_0105_0000$$$::and the dead could not come back to life.[lr]::
6933::$$$message_0048_0105_0001$$$::It wasn't asleep or temporarily out of order.[lr]::
6934::$$$message_0048_0105_0002$$$::[font italic=true]He didn't have it anymore.[font italic=false][lr]::
6935::$$$message_0048_0105_0003$$$::No matter how humanly he lived his life, he would never feel emotion.::
6936::$$$message_0048_0106_0000$$$::It didn't bother him, and it made people think of him as a strong person.[lr]::
6937::$$$message_0048_0106_0001$$$::That wasn't wrong of them.[lr]::
6938::$$$message_0048_0106_0002$$$::...But he did make an effort.[lr]::
6939::$$$message_0048_0106_0003$$$::Even if he was fated to die pointlessly, with a dead heart, walking on coals,[lr]::
6940::$$$message_0048_0106_0004$$$::he tried to live among the people.::
6941::$$$message_0048_0107_0000$$$::   And then, he met a pale woman.[lr]::
6942::$$$message_0048_0107_0001$$$::One day, he was on the way home from work.[lr]::
6943::$$$message_0048_0107_0002$$$::On the way to the mountain gate, he heard a noise from the woods.[lr]::
6944::$$$message_0048_0107_0003$$$::He investigated, out of obligation to those caring for him at the temple, and found a bloody woman.[lr]::
6945::$$$message_0048_0107_0004$$$::Clutching her dark cloak around her, she looked terribly weak, as if she could disappear at any moment.[lr]::
6946::$$$message_0048_0107_0005$$$::Yes, so weak that she might literally disappear, not just die.::
6947::$$$message_0048_0108_0000$$$::   Later, the witch would think...[lr]::
6948::$$$message_0048_0108_0001$$$::Their meeting was a miracle.[lr]::
6949::$$$message_0048_0108_0002$$$::Not just for the witch, though.[lr]::
6950::$$$message_0048_0108_0003$$$::Even if it was just an illusion, something impossible had happened.[lr]::
6951::$$$message_0048_0108_0004$$$::"..."[lr]::
6952::$$$message_0048_0108_0005$$$::His heart had never broken its rhythm in decades, but for an instant, it stopped and restarted.[lr]::
6953::$$$message_0048_0108_0006$$$::Even if it was only a momentary interruption, something which should have been dead stirred back to life.::
6954::$$$message_0048_0109_0000$$$::"What are you doing there?"[lr]::
6955::$$$message_0048_0109_0001$$$::The woman collapsed without responding.[lr]::
6956::$$$message_0048_0109_0002$$$::The mountain forest at night. Rain. A body on death's door. She obviously wasn't a normal person.[lr]::
6957::$$$message_0048_0109_0003$$$::The bloody cloak was trivial.[lr]::
6958::$$$message_0048_0109_0004$$$::This woman was dangerous.[lr]::
6959::$$$message_0048_0109_0005$$$::Someone else would have retreated, but he wasn't like other people. He couldn't have missed the scent of someone like him.::
6960::$$$message_0048_0110_0000$$$::So he took care of the woman.[lr]::
6961::$$$message_0048_0110_0001$$$::He didn't help her because he sensed she was a fellow killer.[lr]::
6962::$$$message_0048_0110_0002$$$::He saved her because she collapsed in front of him.[lr]::
6963::$$$message_0048_0110_0003$$$::That's the only reason he did it.::
6964::$$$message_0048_0111_0000$$$::The woman opened her eyes about an hour later.[lr]::
6965::$$$message_0048_0111_0001$$$::"You're awake. Will you tell me what happened?"[lr]::
6966::$$$message_0048_0111_0002$$$::She stared at him in amazement.[lr]::
6967::$$$message_0048_0111_0003$$$::There was neither bewilderment nor joy.[lr]::
6968::$$$message_0048_0111_0004$$$::Her despair at still being alive threatened to spill out as tears.::
6969::$$$message_0048_0112_0000$$$::"If it's too much trouble, then you can leave. I'll forget this if you want me to."[lr]::
6970::$$$message_0048_0112_0001$$$::How did she take his words?[lr]::
6971::$$$message_0048_0112_0002$$$::Did she think she could use him? Did the act of kindness soften her heart?[lr]::
6972::$$$message_0048_0112_0003$$$::She revealed her origins, and he accepted her extraordinary identity without a second thought.[lr]::
6973::$$$message_0048_0112_0004$$$::Then, he embraced her and decided to participate in the deathmatch she called the Holy Grail War.[lr]::
6974::$$$message_0048_0112_0005$$$::The witch must have been surprised.[lr]::
6975::$$$message_0048_0112_0006$$$::She had begun to recover, just slightly.[lr]::
6976::$$$message_0048_0112_0007$$$::The instant he refused, she would have chuckled and used magecraft to enslave his mind...but with one sentence, he erased her vile scheme.::
6977::$$$message_0048_0113_0000$$$::He didn't agree because he was afraid of the witch, nor because he cared for the Holy Grail.[lr]::
6978::$$$message_0048_0113_0001$$$::He would help the woman because she asked for his help.[lr]::
6979::$$$message_0048_0113_0002$$$::The man never thought killing was evil. He had no reluctance to become her Master.[lr]::
6980::$$$message_0048_0113_0003$$$::It was true, though, that he'd tried to distance himself from his past.[lr]::
6981::$$$message_0048_0113_0004$$$::...If there was something he missed, it was in that moment.[lr]::
6982::$$$message_0048_0113_0005$$$::He never realized the reason he suddenly abandoned his efforts up until now to help the woman.::
6983::$$$message_0048_0114_0000$$$::"Try not to disrupt our current lives. Tell me if you need help."[lr]::
6984::$$$message_0048_0114_0001$$$::That was his direction.[lr]::
6985::$$$message_0048_0114_0002$$$::He had no wish. Only the woman he saved desired the Holy Grail.[lr]::
6986::$$$message_0048_0114_0003$$$::If he fought, it would be for her, not the Grail.[lr]::
6987::$$$message_0048_0114_0004$$$::It was only natural to fulfill his obligation, having promised to help her.[lr]::
6988::$$$message_0048_0114_0005$$$::To him, the Holy Grail War was abnormal, but not evil.[lr]::
6989::$$$message_0048_0114_0006$$$::Rejecting his assigned purpose was evil.::
6990::$$$message_0048_0115_0000$$$::And so, he became the Master of Caster.[lr]::
6991::$$$message_0048_0115_0001$$$::He had no Command Spells, but she obeyed him.[lr]::
6992::$$$message_0048_0115_0002$$$::The man knew nothing of magecraft to begin with. She planned to use him to remain in the mortal world and wield him as a puppet.[lr]::
6993::$$$message_0048_0115_0003$$$::He would not participate in the Holy Grail War. He would leave that to her.[lr]::
6994::$$$message_0048_0115_0004$$$::He would only cut ties with her if she rejected the Holy Grail War.[lr]::
6995::$$$message_0048_0115_0005$$$::Their relationship was harmonious, ideal even, between player and pawn.::
6996::$$$message_0048_0116_0000$$$::But that was all the more reason they did not mesh well as people.[lr]::
6997::$$$message_0048_0116_0001$$$::The more the woman's heart changed, the greater the reason he had to abandon being a Master,[lr]::
6998::$$$message_0048_0116_0002$$$::and as he unconsciously continued to interact with her, he gradually began to fail as a tool.[lr]::
6999::$$$message_0048_0116_0003$$$::...What was this sense of nostalgia?[lr]::
7000::$$$message_0048_0116_0004$$$::It was an emotion that he, with no home to return to, could never[line len=2]should never be allowed to understand.::
7001::$$$message_0048_0117_0000$$$::The war ended quickly.[lr]::
7002::$$$message_0048_0117_0001$$$::An enemy Servant defeated Assassin at the gate, and then her Master lost the ensuing sword fight.[lr]::
7003::$$$message_0048_0117_0002$$$::He lay there, eviscerated.[lr]::
7004::$$$message_0048_0117_0003$$$::His arms, which he'd trained for twenty years, were gone from the elbows down.::
7005::$$$message_0048_0118_0000$$$::"Master! MASTER!!!"[lr]::
7006::$$$message_0048_0118_0001$$$::Her voice echoed throughout the temple grounds.[lr]::
7007::$$$message_0048_0118_0002$$$::The enemy seemed to have departed after finishing the gatekeeper and the Master.[lr]::
7008::$$$message_0048_0118_0003$$$::Left behind, the woman clung madly to her contractor's corpse.[sestop storage=se207.wav time=3000 nowait=1]::
7009::$$$message_0048_0119_0000$$$::He looked at her with unfocused, foggy eyes.[lr]::
7010::$$$message_0048_0119_0001$$$::He saw her tears, and lamented that he'd done something wrong.[lr]::
7011::$$$message_0048_0119_0002$$$::It wasn't a vision caused by his dying delirium.[lr]::
7012::$$$message_0048_0119_0003$$$::A heart he wasn't supposed to have was bleeding at death's door.::
7013::$$$message_0048_0120_0000$$$::The woman's wish was to go home.[lr]::
7014::$$$message_0048_0120_0001$$$::He didn't know where exactly that was.[lr]::
7015::$$$message_0048_0120_0002$$$::Another wave of nostalgia.[lr]::
7016::$$$message_0048_0120_0003$$$::It was a place he'd never seen or heard of before, a fleeting dream that didn't even leave an impression in his mind.[lr]::
7017::$$$message_0048_0120_0004$$$::In the end, he didn't know how to feel about it.::
7018::$$$message_0048_0121_0000$$$::"Get away from here, Caster. That Servant will return if he senses you here."[lr]::
7019::$$$message_0048_0121_0001$$$::His words were impassive.[lr]::
7020::$$$message_0048_0121_0002$$$::His mind was miraculously intact, unlike his body.[lr]::
7021::$$$message_0048_0121_0003$$$::It must have been thanks to his long years of training.[lr]::
7022::$$$message_0048_0121_0004$$$::His consciousness would remain clear until his brain ceased to function.::
7023::$$$message_0048_0122_0000$$$::"What are you saying!? Stay with me! I will heal you, I swear it. I won't let you die, Master...!"[lr]::
7024::$$$message_0048_0122_0001$$$::The woman didn't leave.[lr]::
7025::$$$message_0048_0122_0002$$$::This was rather illogical.[lr]::
7026::$$$message_0048_0122_0003$$$::While it would be a great setback for Caster to lose her Master, her physical host, it wasn't a death sentence.[lr]::
7027::$$$message_0048_0122_0004$$$::She had already lost one Master before this.[lr]::
7028::$$$message_0048_0122_0005$$$::If she feared being attacked again, then she should retreat as soon as possible and make a pact with a new Master.::
7029::$$$message_0048_0123_0000$$$::"Don't underestimate my skills. I am a witch! I can easily patch up a dying human or two...!"[lr]::
7030::$$$message_0048_0123_0001$$$::The miracle didn't happen.[lr]::
7031::$$$message_0048_0123_0002$$$::An enemy Servant destroyed the stored magical energy at Ryudou Temple and inflicted a cursed wound with their Noble Phantasm that couldn't be healed.::
7032::$$$message_0048_0124_0000$$$::"I can...easily... [wvl][move textoff=0 spread=1 mx=234 magnify=1 time=80 my=474 path=(234,474,255,0.91)(234,474,255,1.11) storage=063_血a accel=0]I've done this more times than I can count... [wvl][move textoff=0 spread=1 mx=646 magnify=1.3 time=60 my=390 path=(646,390,255,0.91)(646,390,255,1.11) storage=063_血d accel=0]I won't fail, I won't fail, I won't fail...! [wvl canskip=0 time=400][move textoff=0 spread=1 mx=107 magnify=1.3 time=80 my=354 path=(107,354,255,1.01)(107,354,255,1.11) storage=063_血b accel=0]I've never had any trouble healing something this simple...!"[lr]::
7033::$$$message_0048_0124_0001$$$::Sobbing, the woman chanted her spell like an apology.[lr]::
7034::$$$message_0048_0124_0002$$$::But it didn't work. The divine language she spoke lacked its usual power.[lr]::
7035::$$$message_0048_0124_0003$$$::Minute by minute, grief filled the woman's face.::
7036::$$$message_0048_0125_0000$$$::"Eeeugh, ah, aahh, ah... [wvl][se volume=50 storage=se023.wav]N-no, help, someone, someone pleeeease...! [l][say storage=ryu0220_cas_0191 name=キャスター]Help us, someone help us...![lr]::
7037::$$$message_0048_0125_0001$$$::This can't be happening! I've, I've never failed at this before! NEVER...!!!"::
7038::$$$message_0048_0126_0000$$$::It was too late to heal the wound, too late to revive his flesh.[lr]::
7039::$$$message_0048_0126_0001$$$::She couldn't save anything.[lr]::
7040::$$$message_0048_0126_0002$$$::The witch's only role was to debase others.[lr]::
7041::$$$message_0048_0126_0003$$$::She could heal people or animate the dead, but she was simply unable to [font italic=true]save[font italic=false] them.[lr]::
7042::$$$message_0048_0126_0004$$$::...It must be because she had never genuinely tried to save anyone before.[lr]::
7043::$$$message_0048_0126_0005$$$::Up until now, she was unaware of that rule.::
7044::$$$message_0048_0127_0000$$$::"Ah... Aahh, [wvl][se volume=40 storage=se023.wav]AAAAHHHHH...!"[lr]::
7045::$$$message_0048_0127_0001$$$::Magecraft wouldn't work.[lr]::
7046::$$$message_0048_0127_0002$$$::She could cry for help, but none would come.[lr]::
7047::$$$message_0048_0127_0003$$$::She looks up. The sky is distant. She can't stop the warmth from leaving his body.::
7048::$$$message_0048_0128_0000$$$::"No... Don't...die. Don't die, don't die, don't die, Souichirou...!!!"[lr]::
7049::$$$message_0048_0128_0001$$$::He hears her sobbing.[lr]::
7050::$$$message_0048_0128_0002$$$::Her crying face gives him a headache.[lr]::
7051::$$$message_0048_0128_0003$$$::He knows it's because she is sad, and finally accepts that he was unable to become a tool.::
7052::$$$message_0048_0129_0000$$$::...He thought he'd just live normally.[lr]::
7053::$$$message_0048_0129_0001$$$::When he killed someone and became free, he thought that he had no choice but to live out his remaining life.[lr]::
7054::$$$message_0048_0129_0002$$$::   What a bold-faced lie that was.[lr]::
7055::$$$message_0048_0129_0003$$$::He simply didn't admit that he regretted it.[lr]::
7056::$$$message_0048_0129_0004$$$::His meaningless twenty years, and the person he killed had always lingered in his heart.[lr]::
7057::$$$message_0048_0129_0005$$$::He'd always thought that it was wrong to kill someone when he only knew their name.::
7058::$$$message_0048_0130_0000$$$::             ...He wasn't born to be an assassin, had not made that choice himself.[lr]::
7059::$$$message_0048_0130_0001$$$::             ...He didn't grow up to be the person he wanted to be.::
7060::$$$message_0048_0131_0000$$$::How could he make up for that mistake...?[lr]::
7061::$$$message_0048_0131_0001$$$::It was fun.[lr]::
7062::$$$message_0048_0131_0002$$$::It was easy to train single-mindedly to master a single technique, to stop thinking and be a tool.[lr]::
7063::$$$message_0048_0131_0003$$$::He was so focused on that, never bothering to look back, that he erased two lives.[lr]::
7064::$$$message_0048_0131_0004$$$::What could be more evil than that?[lr]::
7065::$$$message_0048_0131_0005$$$::Even if part of the blame lay with those who raised him...[lr]::
7066::$$$message_0048_0131_0006$$$::Even if he did not know what it was for...[lr]::
7067::$$$message_0048_0131_0007$$$::He had slain someone with his own hands.::
7068::$$$message_0048_0132_0000$$$::He left that life because he didn't know how to make up for it.[lr]::
7069::$$$message_0048_0132_0001$$$::He stopped training the only art that gave his life any meaning, and gently immersed himself in a peaceful existence.[lr]::
7070::$$$message_0048_0132_0002$$$::He wished for nothing and obtained nothing.[lr]::
7071::$$$message_0048_0132_0003$$$::This was the best atonement he could think of.::
7072::$$$message_0048_0133_0000$$$::...And that life fell apart once he met this woman.[lr]::
7073::$$$message_0048_0133_0001$$$::This pale woman, lost in the cold rain.[lr]::
7074::$$$message_0048_0133_0002$$$::She was simply beautiful.[lr]::
7075::$$$message_0048_0133_0003$$$::More beautiful than any woman he'd ever seen.[lr]::
7076::$$$message_0048_0133_0004$$$::That was the only reason.[lr]::
7077::$$$message_0048_0133_0005$$$::He extended his hand to something beautiful.[lr]::
7078::$$$message_0048_0133_0006$$$::Looking back...[lr]::
7079::$$$message_0048_0133_0007$$$::The fact that he managed to turn his back on his daily atonement and become a source of strength to her was surely...::
7080::$$$message_0048_0134_0000$$$::"I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry..."[lr]::
7081::$$$message_0048_0134_0001$$$::Her voice had changed to quiet weeping.[lr]::
7082::$$$message_0048_0134_0002$$$::What he thought was rain was something warmer.[lr]::
7083::$$$message_0048_0134_0003$$$::The woman would not leave.[lr]::
7084::$$$message_0048_0134_0004$$$::Just like that night, her blood-soaked hands clung to his chest.[lr]::
7085::$$$message_0048_0134_0005$$$::He thought it was truly sad that he couldn't see her face anymore.::
7086::$$$message_0048_0135_0000$$$::"...I see. I realize it now."[lr]::
7087::$$$message_0048_0135_0001$$$::Too late, but there was still some time left.[lr]::
7088::$$$message_0048_0135_0002$$$::...He must have wanted to apologize for something.[lr]::
7089::$$$message_0048_0135_0003$$$::For the things he regretted.[lr]::
7090::$$$message_0048_0135_0004$$$::For the things he had to ask forgiveness for.::
7091::$$$message_0048_0136_0000$$$::   For a long time,[lr]::
7092::$$$message_0048_0136_0001$$$::I've always had the vague desire...[lr]::
7093::$$$message_0048_0136_0002$$$::      To live for someone else.[lr]::
7094::$$$message_0048_0136_0003$$$::Such a simple desire...::
7095::$$$message_0048_0137_0000$$$::"Caster."[lr]::
7096::$$$message_0048_0137_0001$$$::The woman wouldn't leave.[lr]::
7097::$$$message_0048_0137_0002$$$::Death's footsteps could approach at any moment.::
7098::$$$message_0048_0138_0000$$$::"I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry..."[lr]::
7099::$$$message_0048_0138_0001$$$::She seemed to be apologizing to herself.[lr]::
7100::$$$message_0048_0138_0002$$$::...It was enough.[lr]::
7101::$$$message_0048_0138_0003$$$::He couldn't apologize anymore, but she did it in his stead.[lr]::
7102::$$$message_0048_0138_0004$$$::There was only one remaining concern: [lr]::
7103::$$$message_0048_0138_0005$$$::He had to release this beautiful bird back to her home.::
7104::$$$message_0048_0139_0000$$$::"Caster."[lr]::
7105::$$$message_0048_0139_0001$$$::She would never leave his side.[lr]::
7106::$$$message_0048_0139_0002$$$::In that moment, he can no longer see, yet his heart is more tranquil than ever.[lr]::
7107::$$$message_0048_0139_0003$$$::"...It's all right, just go already.[lr]::
7108::$$$message_0048_0139_0004$$$::You can't be here."[lr]::
7109::$$$message_0048_0139_0005$$$::He tells the grieving woman, ready to forgive everything.::
7110::$$$message_0048_0140_0000$$$::...Wherever she flew off to is already a distant tale.[lr]::
7111::$$$message_0048_0140_0001$$$::She wasn't the woman he thought she was.[lr]::
7112::$$$message_0048_0140_0002$$$::The conclusion wasn't the one he wished for.::
7113::$$$message_0048_0141_0000$$$::Thus ended the tale of a decrepit killer and a witch.[lr]::
7114::$$$message_0048_0141_0001$$$::If there was one bit of salvation...[lr]::
7115::$$$message_0048_0141_0002$$$::...it was that brief period after the two met.[lr]::
7116::$$$message_0048_0141_0003$$$::Their life together lasted less than a month, but it was far more human, more gentle, than anything they'd ever experienced.::
7117::$$$message_0048_0142_0000$$$::                                          She blinks out of her stupor.[lr]::
7118::$$$message_0048_0142_0001$$$::                                          It appears she was daydreaming.::
7119::$$$message_0048_0143_0000$$$::"........."[lr]::
7120::$$$message_0048_0143_0001$$$::The black-robed witch is free of the summer rain.[lr]::
7121::$$$message_0048_0143_0002$$$::She blinks away the dizziness and gazes up at the gloomy sky.::
7122::$$$message_0048_0144_0000$$$::"Don't make promises you can't keep.[lr]::
7123::$$$message_0048_0144_0001$$$::I never had any wings to begin with."[lr]::
7124::$$$message_0048_0144_0002$$$::But it must have seemed that way, to him.[lr]::
7125::$$$message_0048_0144_0003$$$::Wings are light even when falling to the earth.[lr]::
7126::$$$message_0048_0144_0004$$$::Perhaps he thought she would someday shake off the mud and return to the sky.::
7127::$$$message_0048_0145_0000$$$::"...Honestly, he's so insensitive. There are migratory birds who become so fond of their stops that they forget to move on.[lr]::
7128::$$$message_0048_0145_0001$$$::I wish he'd come up with a convenient excuse like that."[lr]::
7129::$$$message_0048_0145_0002$$$::She smiles, talking to herself.[lr]::
7130::$$$message_0048_0145_0003$$$::The witch slowly closes her eyes, as if falling asleep.[lr]::
7131::$$$message_0048_0145_0004$$$::As if to take a moment in time and bury it in her dreams.[lr]::
7132::$$$message_0048_0145_0005$$$::She will have to wake up from this dream, someday. But she will savor it in the meantime.[nolr][p]::
7133::$$$message_0048_0145_0006$$$::   This too, is a fragment.[lr]::
7134::$$$message_0048_0145_0007$$$::It passes by and lodges itself in one's breast, while the moment in time flows on without resistance.[lr]::
7135::$$$message_0048_0145_0008$$$::With the heart alone, it has nowhere to stay,[lr]::
7136::$$$message_0048_0145_0009$$$::and with the body alone, it leaves no trace.[lr]::
7137::$$$message_0048_0145_0010$$$::In this paradise, at least, they still sing of the spring that never came, even if there is no one to hear it.[nolr][p]::
906909::$$$message_9048_0098_0004$$$::he concluded, and with that, settled his own account.[r]::

